    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nIs there or will there be support for default keybindings (e.g. `d` or `y`) and something like a `g?` for exploring all Normal mode keybindings? It might be an issue with my setup but I couldn't find any information on this in the docs or anywhere online.\r\n\r\nThanks.",
